endobj

165 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 62 0 R/E(Traditional markets are the soul of Seoul's food scene. Gwangjang Market is famous for bindaetteok and raw fish. Namdaemun Market offers affordable street snacks and local produce. Tongin Market lets you fill a lunchbox with traditional side dishes using old-style coins. Arrive early for the freshest picks and fewest crowds.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

166 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 62 0 R/E(Hands-on cooking classes are a must for food lovers. Learn to make kimchi and bibimbap with local instructors in central Seoul. Book classes through Airbnb Experiences or Klook for easy English-language options. Most classes run 2-3 hours and include a full meal. Look for market food tours that combine shopping with cooking for the ultimate immersive experience.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

